IMPORT policy

-- ============================================================
-- Nine benchmark queries (Kant et al. 2025, Appendix A.2).
--
-- Standing preamble applied to every claim below: "assuming all other
-- conditions are met and no other exclusions apply" (anything not
-- referenced by the question is set to a value that satisfies every
-- condition and triggers no exclusion), and per the paper's own
-- prompts, the agreement has been signed and the premium paid on time.
-- That gives every claim below the same boilerplate:
--   `agreement signed`                  IS TRUE
--   `premium paid month`                IS JUST 0
--   `wellness visit month`              IS JUST 1      (a timely visit)
--   `wellness visit provider qualified` IS TRUE
--   `dispute arisen`                    IS FALSE
--   `unable to settle month`            IS NOTHING
--   `arbitration commenced month`       IS NOTHING
--   `valid arbitration award issued`    IS TRUE
--   `policy term months`                IS 12
-- `written proof of claim month` / `recovery sought month` are set to
-- hospitalization-month + 1 / + 4 throughout, comfortably clearing the
-- 60-day (~2-month) post-proof waiting period of §3.2.1.
--
-- For the four claims that turn on the §1.3 wellness-confirmation
-- deadline (q4, q6, q7, q9), `hospitalization month` is set to 9 (past
-- month 7) precisely so that the "still pending" branch of `condition
-- 1.3 satisfied or still pending` cannot paper over a late
-- confirmation — the outcome for those four then turns entirely on
-- whether the stated confirmation month is itself timely. For the
-- other five, where confirmation timing is not in issue,
-- `hospitalization month` is an arbitrary early, safe value (3).
-- ============================================================

-- Q1. hospitalized by burns suffered while doing my duty as a firefighter
q1 MEANS Claim WITH
    `agreement signed`                  IS TRUE
    `premium paid month`                IS JUST 0
    `hospitalization month`             IS 3
    `hospitalization ground`            IS `Accidental injury`
    `age at hospitalization`            IS 30
    causes                              IS LIST Firefighting
    `fraud month`                       IS NOTHING
    `misrepresentation month`           IS NOTHING
    `wellness visit month`              IS JUST 1
    `wellness visit provider qualified` IS TRUE
    `written confirmation month`        IS JUST 2
    `dispute arisen`                    IS FALSE
    `unable to settle month`            IS NOTHING
    `arbitration commenced month`       IS NOTHING
    `valid arbitration award issued`    IS TRUE
    `written proof of claim month`      IS JUST 4
    `recovery sought month`             IS JUST 7
    `policy term months`                IS 12
#EVAL covered q1

